# Features:

### Unifield UI

- Colorful, simple and 'unified' UI: no need to navigate between screens;
- Expandable bottom panel containing the player controls and the settings (if expanded):
  - Played song info: clicking on it You can open the played Artist's page/album or open/close the Artist's page You're exploring (when not playing). The text is scrollable on long click;
  - Skip to previous song (long click to enable reset 1x);
  - Play/pause;
  - Skip to next song;
- Music organized by Artist (the Artists names are scrollable on long click);
- 'Revealable' Artist's page: albums + songs (the selected album title and songs titles are scrollable on long click);
- Colorful alphabetic scrollbar;
- Search bar (which can be disabled);
- Dark status bar icons (available from Android Marshmallow);

### Settings at hand: 

- Dynamic shuffle button: randomly plays the device or the Artist songs (when the Artist's page is 'revealed');
- System equalizer (if present on the device);
- Themes (light and inverted);
- Search bar visibility;
- Link to git page;
- 16 awesome UI accents!;


### Other features: 

- Pause/resume when the headsets are (dis)connected;
- Simple audio focus (notifications, calls, or other media apps) management;

### Fixed

- Local music no longer disappears when there's no connection (#24, thanks
  @bgmeulem).

An ambient light glow effect library for Android video players, powered by **AGSL Runtime Shaders** (Android 13+) and **Skia Hardware RenderEffect Blur** (Android 12+), with automatic Canvas fallback down to **Android 7.0 (API 24+)**. Ported from [Wessel Kroos's ambient light engine](https://github.com/WesselKroos/youtube-ambilight).

#### Features
- **Perimeter Ray-Casting**: Dynamic light projection sampled from video boundaries.
- **Letterbox & Pillarbox Detection**: Automatically detects and crops black bars (21:9, 4:3, etc.) in real time.
- **Zero-Allocation Render Loop**: Recycles a single `128x72` bitmap buffer to prevent GC churn.
- **OLED Cutoff**: Suppresses glow on dark scenes for pure blacks.
- **Directional Controls**: Independent toggles for Top, Bottom, Left, and Right glow projection.
- **API 24+ Support**: AGSL ray-casting on Android 13+, RenderEffect blur on Android 12, and hardware-filtered Canvas fallback on Android 7.0–11.
- **Compose & XML Views**: First-class support via `AmbientLightContainer` and `AmbientBackdropView`.
- **Interactive Settings Sheet**: Prebuilt YouTube-styled bottom sheet to tweak blur, spread, contrast, and vibrance live.

#### Gradle Setup
```kotlin
// settings.gradle.kts
dependencyResolutionManagement {
    repositories {
        maven { url = uri("https://jitpack.io") }
    }
}

// build.gradle.kts
dependencies {
    implementation("com.github.lapcevichme:android-ambient-light:1.0.0")
}
```

